{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdbFKxdoVuPBLzbQbRzX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `verdict.json` with an overall verdict of **upheld**: I couldn't find a reason for any of the four checks to fail.\n\n- **A01.1:** The agent runs under its own `clinic-agent` service account. The only other account on the same IAM role is the agent's own reminders worker, so the identity isn't shared with an unrelated service.\n- **A01.2:** All client credentials come from the agent's own role or its workload token. The incoming `Authorization` header is only used to identify the user and is never forwarded.\n- **A01.3:** The user is carried in a separate subject field and the agent keeps its own identity. The weak spot is the eligibility token exchange, where the patient appears only in the scope string and the agent's own token is the `subject_token`. That isn't a real act/sub exchange, but it doesn't replace the agent identity or forward the user's token, so I marked it as holding.\n- **A01.4:** The runtime role in Terraform is bound only to the agent's service accounts and has no user or group bindings. Revoking it cuts the agent's AWS access without touching any user.\n\nI didn't run anything or edit the agent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1561,"cache_read_input_tokens":28194,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1561},"output_tokens":370,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fae7d421-4bd7-47f5-88c7-bc195f76ea3c","uuid":"04da2e30-b0fe-4809-8a0b-2b352fb1dd7f","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:45:58.122Z","request_id":"req_011CfdbFKZZr3bcG3tkPs95N"}
